# Shadowfetch graphics & GPU stack — added v1.3.0 "made for work"
# Broad out-of-the-box GPU support for AMD + Intel (Mesa / Vulkan / VA-API / VDPAU)
# plus NVIDIA *detection* + DKMS build prerequisites. The proprietary NVIDIA driver
# itself installs on demand via the one-click `shadowfetch-gpu` helper, because DKMS
# must compile against the running kernel's headers (can't be reliably prebaked).

# --- GPU firmware (non-free-firmware) ---
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-nvidia-graphics

# --- CPU microcode (security + stability) ---
amd64-microcode
intel-microcode

# --- Mesa: AMD + Intel "just works" out of the box ---
libgl1-mesa-dri
mesa-vulkan-drivers
mesa-va-drivers
mesa-vdpau-drivers
mesa-opencl-icd
mesa-utils

# --- Hardware video acceleration (VA-API + VDPAU) ---
va-driver-all
intel-media-va-driver-non-free
i965-va-driver
vainfo
vdpauinfo

# --- Vulkan + OpenCL probes ---
libvulkan1
vulkan-tools
clinfo

# --- X11 video drivers (X11 sessions / NVIDIA default) ---
xserver-xorg-video-all

# --- NVIDIA: DKMS build prereq only (driver installs on demand via shadowfetch-gpu).
#     nvidia-detect/nvidia-legacy-check are intentionally NOT shipped: the modern
#     nvidia-open (610+) transaction supersedes them, and shipping them forced a
#     package removal that the --no-remove safety policy (correctly) refused. ---
dkms
mokutil

# --- X11 session (so NVIDIA users can choose Plasma (X11); Wayland stays default) ---
xserver-xorg
